{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/383010-what-do-you-think-of-bayonetta-lunar-thread-enter-at-own-risks","id":383010,"title":"What do you think of Bayonetta? [Lunar thread, enter at own risks]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-27T06:33:01-08:00","id":383010,"title":"What do you think of Bayonetta? [Lunar thread, enter at own risks]","content":"So, a few weeks ago we had a discussion about Alex Mercer and his implementation as a Lunar. Most agreed that while some of his powers could be used as stunt fodders or could be one way to look at the charms of a lunar, his aesthetics and story were not.<br /> <br /> Now what do we think of Bayonetta? Raw sexuality and dexterity, moon-themed, shapeshifting into animals, everything she does comes with a burst of magic, etc...<br /> <br /> I believe that the character is a good example of a 2nd edition lunar (since we know nothing about third edition Lunars).<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T06:49:01-08:00","id":383034,"title":"","content":"I'd see a No-Moon pulling off similar antics - walking on walls, seeming to bend time (in a Lunar's case more like &quot;Focusing really hard and experiencing bullet-time&quot; with Mental Attribute charms) and calling upon lunar imagery for various effects (White Reaper Style?).<br /> <br /> Her hair could be a particular example of Terrifying Mane mixed with some custom shapeshifting charms or a particular brand of Sorcery (like the idea of summoning animals out of tattoos, but with hair).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:41:23-08:00","id":383092,"title":"","content":"In Second Edition, she was a good example of a Lunar, because Lunar themes were so confused that &quot;defying gravity&quot; and &quot;manipulating time&quot; weren't out of place.<br /> <br /> In Third Edition? Fata-Ku is right in that &quot;bullet time&quot; can be a result of just being Very Fast. The magical hair could be the awesome result of a Sorcerous Working she did to herself. The Witchwalk could be an Evocation or basic effect of artifact high-heels, or perhaps another Sorcerous Working.<br /> <br /> Bayonetta definitely seems to have a Totem and Tell going, what with her Giant Butterfly shadow. She can even turn into a swarm of the things, so she's covered for her Spirit Shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:54:54-08:00","id":383107,"title":"","content":"Haven't played the games, all I've got to go off of is Yahtzee's review of it, and I have no idea how accurate that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:57:28-08:00","id":383110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/383010-what-do-you-think-of-bayonetta-lunar-thread-enter-at-own-risks?p=383107#post383107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't played the games, all I've got to go off of is Yahtzee's review of it, and I have no idea how accurate that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing out on a neat visual experience.<br /> <br /> At least watch some of the Let's Plays on youtube. The boss battles can be amazing, and good inspiration for Exalted duels against giant creatures in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:13:18-08:00","id":383126,"title":"","content":"I don't really expect to see Lunars in 3rd edition doing much in the way of Bayonetta. Bayonetta is, first and foremost, a witch. She's very much magic in all her aesthetics, with sorcerous power basically gushing around as she attacks with materialized constructs and weapons from thin air, witchfire increasing her reach and power and an Umbran seal that looks most definitely hermetic-ish. Not quite the thing that devs seem to be going for.<br /> <br /> With a bit of stretching and some custom charms you might be able to fit her in Lunars 2nd, though,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T13:47:09-08:00","id":383543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the creator of the Prototype thread, I'd like to mention that that thread was intended to be about James Heller, not Mercer\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026yet you referred to the thread, calling it there and even here, a <i>Prototype</i> thread, as opposed to a <i>Prototype 2</i> thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And with that misconception cleaned up, I leave this thread forever to avoid derailing. </div> </div> </div>Time will tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T14:28:00-08:00","id":383596,"title":"","content":"I never saw her as a Lunar. The hair-morphing effects always came across as very Infernal to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T15:00:25-08:00","id":383624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/383010-what-do-you-think-of-bayonetta-lunar-thread-enter-at-own-risks?p=383596#post383596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never saw her as a Lunar. The hair-morphing effects always came across as very Infernal to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shapeshifting into butterflies, panther, raven, and having moon-based powers struck you as Infernal powers?<br /> <br /> Did I missed a Yozi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T15:18:03-08:00","id":383644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/383010-what-do-you-think-of-bayonetta-lunar-thread-enter-at-own-risks?p=383624#post383624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifting into butterflies, panther, raven, and having moon-based powers struck you as Infernal powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about the first game or the second one?<br /> <br /> Sprouting butterfly wings != turning into a butterfly. And yes the crazy hair finishers read much more as transhuman Infernal than they did animal-focused Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T15:40:48-08:00","id":383689,"title":"","content":"Bayonetta's dodge involved turning into a small swarm of butterflies in the first game. In the second game, it seems like she slow fall by growing a large pair of butterfly wings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T16:22:47-08:00","id":383761,"title":"","content":"I haven't played these games either, but what you're describing sounds very much like a Terrifying Argent Witch.... probably a New Moon favoring Dexterity and Appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T20:12:16-08:00","id":383926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/383010-what-do-you-think-of-bayonetta-lunar-thread-enter-at-own-risks?p=383644#post383644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about the first game or the second one?<br /> <br /> Sprouting butterfly wings != turning into a butterfly. And yes the crazy hair finishers read much more as transhuman Infernal than they did animal-focused Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both her summoning demon and her shapeshifting power are actually not her native magic, it's trick that she gains by making pact with the denizen of hell, so I agree with her having more Infernal/Malfeas flavor than Lunar.<br /> <br /> And beside, she's only turning into animal for like 5-10% of the game, but since Lunar has no clear theme at all, it seem that having something vaguely animal-related is enough for people to scream inspiration.<br /> <br /> The way she instantly knows how to competently use all the Artifact Odin gave her, plus her ability to unlock Evocation on all of them, I would say that she's a Solar. We even have a bullet time charm in Solar Awareness !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 01-27-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T20:31:36-08:00","id":383932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/383010-what-do-you-think-of-bayonetta-lunar-thread-enter-at-own-risks?p=383126#post383126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really expect to see Lunars in 3rd edition doing much in the way of Bayonetta. Bayonetta is, first and foremost, a witch. She's very much magic in all her aesthetics, with sorcerous power basically gushing around as she attacks with materialized constructs and weapons from thin air, witchfire increasing her reach and power and an Umbran seal that looks most definitely hermetic-ish. Not quite the thing that devs seem to be going for.<br /> <br /> With a bit of stretching and some custom charms you might be able to fit her in Lunars 2nd, though,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see how she can't be a Lunar with sorcery. It's not like a Lunar can't be a &quot;witch&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T06:18:34-08:00","id":384164,"title":"","content":"She could also be a Lunar with a Sword (and/or other) Grace and some mojo that allows her to Shape in Creation (like... Style 5 or N/A) or use hair-themed Invocation Charms (Elemental Shape: Hair? It's legit for Changeling...) for Behemoth Familiars.<br /> <br /> Having &quot;sorcerous power basically gushing around as she attacks&quot; is not any more difficult for an exalt than having a bunch of Obvious charms and/or an Anima Flaring at the Iconic level. E.g. iirc Long-arm Technique increases one's reach with Essence flares beyond a certain point - though I don't remember the Errata for it if there was one. Also Celestial/Sidereal martial arts.<br /> <br /> Sure, other splats can <i>also</i> model her, I'd go with Fairfolk personally (the visual flair and constructs is totally an Entertainer-Warrior using Fantasies and Glamours).<br /> <br /> * (dammit, I can't wait for lunars to get better treatment than &quot;ah fukkit, let's copy-paste solar charms that have animals in their name&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T18:22:42-08:00","id":384671,"title":"","content":"Her familiars are specifically demons she made pacts with, her hair acts as a portal for then to come through, they are not actually <i>made</i> of hair. The Butterfly wings and shadow are due to her main pact being Madam Butterfly, the demon who's fists and feet you see as combo enders. Also she turns into bats when she dodges not butterflies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T18:44:08-08:00","id":384681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/383010-what-do-you-think-of-bayonetta-lunar-thread-enter-at-own-risks?p=384164#post384164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, other splats can <i>also</i> model her, I'd go with Fairfolk personally (the visual flair and constructs is totally an Entertainer-Warrior using Fantasies and Glamours).</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone I know once compared the game to what would happen if a powerful noble raksha went to war with a spirit court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}